// SwaggerInfo holds exported Swagger Info so clients can modify it
var SwaggerInfo = &swag.Spec{
	Version:          "1.0",
	Host:             "",
	BasePath:         "/api/v1",
	Schemes:          []string{"http", "https"},
	Title:            "LoKey: True Random Number Generation Service API",
	Description:      "LoKey is a high-availability, high-bandwidth true random number generation service named after Loki, the Norse god of chaos, reflecting the unpredictable nature of true randomness. This project provides affordable and accessible hardware-based true randomness through off-the-shelf components with a Go implementation.\n\n## Hardware Architecture\nThe system targets Raspberry Pi 5 (ARM64) and x86_64 hosts with one or more ATECC608A chips. Local development uses CONTROLLER_MODE=emulated (crypto/rand) without hardware. Production uses hardware TRNG via I2C.\n\n## System Architecture\nLoKey consists of four microservices:\n- **Controller Service**: Interfaces with the ATECC608A chip to harvest true random numbers and process SHA-256 hashes\n- **Fortuna Service**: Amplifies the entropy using the Fortuna algorithm for enhanced randomness\n- **VirtIO Service**: Provides high-performance random data access for virtualization via named pipe (FIFO) and HTTP streaming, serving VMs/containers\n- **API Service**: Provides endpoints for configuration, data retrieval from TRNG and Fortuna, and VirtIO seeding management. Entropy queues are held in memory only (`memory://channels`); there is no on-disk database.. Entropy queues are held in memory only (`memory://channels`); there is no on-disk database.\n\n## VirtIO endpoints (via Traefik prefix /virtio)\nThe VirtIO microservice is exposed separately (not under /api/v1):\n- GET /virtio/health — VirtIO health\n- GET /virtio/info — status + pipe path + queue stats\n- GET /virtio/config/queue — queue depth and counters\n- GET /virtio/generate?count=1 — pull seeded entropy (hex)\n- GET /virtio/stream — chunked octet-stream for VMs/containers\n- POST /virtio/seed — seed queue (used by the API seeder)\n- GET /api/v1/config/virtio — seeding source / queue size (API)\n- GET /api/v1/status — includes virtio queue + quality metrics\n\n## Use Cases\nThis service is valuable for cryptographic key generation, password management, blockchain applications, Monte Carlo simulations, gaming systems, IoT device authentication, secure communications, financial services, and scientific research requiring provably random data.\n\n## Data Formats\nSupports multiple output formats: int8, int16, int32, int64, uint8, uint16, uint32, uint64, and raw binary data with configurable chunk sizes and pagination.\n\n## Repository & Support\nFor issues, feature requests, contributions, and detailed hardware setup instructions, visit: https://github.com/LokeyTRaaS/Lokey\nFor more information about the OSS initiative, please visit our website: https://lokey.cloud",
	InfoInstanceName: "swagger",
	SwaggerTemplate:  docTemplate,
	LeftDelim:        "{{",
	RightDelim:       "}}",
}

